<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 March, from 630 to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraclius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/630">630 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,396 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius restores the True Cross to Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition on this day, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> returned the relic of the cross, captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> in 614, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. Within a decade the city fell to the Arab armies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross">True Cross</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1556">1556 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">470 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Cranmer burned at the stake in Oxford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-common-prayer">Book of Common Prayer</a>, withdrew his recantations before Mary I's officials. He thrust the hand that had signed them into the flames first.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1788">1788 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Great fire destroys much of New Orleans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Good Friday fire burned 856 buildings in the Spanish colonial city. With a second fire in 1794, it led to the rebuilding of the French Quarter in brick and tile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pius VII crowned pope in Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> occupied by the French, the cardinals met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii">Barnaba Chiaramonti</a> was crowned Pope Pius VII. He later signed a concordat with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and was held captive by him.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany launches its Spring Offensive</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Michael struck British lines on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Somme</a> after a five-hour bombardment, gaining more ground in days than any attack since 1914. It ran out of steam, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> counter-attacked that summer.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Police kill 69 protesters at Sharpeville</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">South African police fired on an unarmed crowd protesting against the pass laws, killing 69 people. The government banned the ANC and PAC, and 21 March is now Human Rights Day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
